Strict alignment: regions take in loops and returns (applies after perf-81).

perf-81 grows a region only by blocks whose predecessors are all in it already, so it cannot take in a
loop: the header's back edge comes from a block that has not joined yet. The JIT also hoists invariant
work out of loops, so the header often holds no access through the base, and the base's accesses in the
loop body kept a test per iteration. Return blocks could not join either, so the block that reads the
last value and returns kept its own test.

The region is now the largest single-entry set of blocks: it starts as every block the entry reaches
through blocks that can join, then drops each block a predecessor outside the region enters, until no
block is. Loops whose back edges stay in the region join whole. As before, no block of the region stores
the base or its parent struct, so the base keeps the tested value around the loop, and a jump back to
the entry tests again; another base is covered only when no region block stores it. A return block
(other than the merged return block) can join as well; its clone returns too. Whether a block leads to an
access is now found by a fixpoint, since the region may have cycles. The other conditions are perf-81's:
no EH regions, only nodes perf-80 clones, single entry and the clone budget.

    entry:                     ; perf-81 tested again in every iteration and after the loop
      andi  t, base, size-1
      bnez  t, slow
      access
    loop:
      access                   ; no test
      bnez  i, loop
      access                   ; no test
      ret

Nethermind stateless guest on SP1 (sp1-runner v6.6.0), on top of perf-76..81, cycles:
  block 26055159:  96,097,609 ->  96,065,170 (-0.03%), gas -0.01%
  block 26112793: 209,036,962 -> 208,977,814 (-0.03%), gas -0.01%
  block 11940631 (Glamsterdam): 607,594,579 -> 607,490,774 (-0.02%), gas -0.01%
  outputs identical. The SP1 guest ELF grows by 16 KB (+0.2%).
Only builds with JitRiscV64StrictAlign change: the ZisK guest builds byte-identical.
Regression test: tools/tests/StrictAlignment/FastPath.

